# ASSET-ACCEPTANCE POLICY v3 (user rule): public/assets/ holds ONLY accepted,
# committed running assets — normal git content with no ignore rules. New or
# pending binaries land in public/staging/ (gitignored, still web-served, so
# the game runs them for evaluation: loaders try /assets/... first, then
# /staging/...). Acceptance is a plain file move:
#   mv public/staging/<x> public/assets/<x> && git add public/assets/<x>
# (no -f needed). Never drop a new binary directly into public/assets/ —
# auto-commits would sweep it in unreviewed.
/public/staging/
# raw asset packs + platform/local junk
/assets/
tmp/
.initial_snapshot.json

# one-off diagnostic scripts (kept local, never committed)
/scripts/tmp/

# draco benchmark scratch output (scripts/make-draco-demo-glb.ts)
scripts/.tmp/
